<h2 id="faq">Frequently asked questions</h2>

<h3>What are the most important ecommerce KPIs?</h3>
<p>The most important ones are conversion rate, average order value, customer acquisition cost, return on ad spend, customer lifetime value, repeat purchase rate and gross margin. Together they show whether you are attracting buyers, whether each sale is profitable and whether customers come back.</p>

<h3>What is a good ecommerce conversion rate?</h3>
<p>It varies widely by industry, price point and traffic source, so compare your store with its own history first. Many stores see conversion rates in the low single digits. A steady upward trend matters more than hitting a particular number.</p>

<h3>How often should I review ecommerce analytics?</h3>
<p>Check headline numbers such as revenue, orders and ad spend daily or weekly, and review deeper metrics such as customer lifetime value, repeat rate and margin monthly. A short weekly review with the same dashboard each time works best.</p>

<h3>Which tool is best for ecommerce analytics?</h3>
<p>Start with the analytics built into your store platform and Google Analytics 4. When you need to combine store, advertising and finance data in one view, a BI tool such as Power BI is a strong next step.</p>

